Explanation of the code

*Server(Server.exe):

The server starts by initializing Winsock (WSAStartup) to use sockets in Windows
It creates a server socket that listens on port 5000.
After starting to listen, it enters an infinite loop that accepts new clients using accept()
For each client that connects:
Give it a unique ID (A, B, C...) based on the order of connection
Add the client to a map that links the ID to the SOCKET
Send a welcome message to the client with its ID
Create a new thread (handle_client) to handle messages from that client
Each client thread:
Reads messages from the client 
Splits the message in a format
Sends the message only to the right client, showing who sent it (From A: ...), Can also send a public message.

*Client (Client.exe):

The client also starts by initializing Winsock and creating a socket.
Connects to the server at 127.0.0.1 : 5000.
After connecting, it starts a thread to receive messages( receive_messages) that prints every message received:
If the message is "Your ID is : X" – it saves its ID 
Otherwise – it prints the message with the sender’s name
In the main loop of the client:
The user types a message in the format <recipientID>:<message>
Sends the message to the server with send().
